msgid "List available reference filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1556
msgid ""
"Returns the values this site can filter references by: the three taxonomies "
"with their terms, plus the customers and locations. Call this before jpkcom-"
"acf-references/query-references so term slugs and post IDs never have to be "
"guessed. Also reports how many published references the public listing rule "
"excludes and why."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1586
msgid ""
"Every reference-type term, whether or not a reference currently uses it. "
"Filter with the slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1587
msgid "Every reference-filter-1 term."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1588
msgid "Every reference-filter-2 term."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1589
msgid "Published customers, as accepted by the \"customer\" filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1590
msgid "Published locations, as accepted by the \"location\" filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1591
msgid ""
"True when at least one list above was cut off at this site's reporting "
"limit, so it is not the complete vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1592
msgid ""
"Front-end archive URL for references, empty when the post type has none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1595
msgid ""
"Site-level counts, not counts for any particular query. published = all "
"published references; listed = those the public listing shows; the two "
"hidden_* numbers are the difference and partition the remainder exactly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1597
msgid "Published references, regardless of the listing rule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1598
msgid "References the public listing shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1599
msgid "Excluded because their expiry date has passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1600
msgid ""
"Excluded because they carry no reference_featured meta row at all. The row's "
"value is irrelevant; a stored 0 is listed, a missing row is not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1603
msgid "Locale these labels were read in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1613
msgid "Query references"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1614
msgid ""
"Runs a filtered, paginated query over the references this site lists "
"publicly and returns compact records. Only values reported by jpkcom-acf-"
"references/list-filters are accepted; anything else is reported back under "
"\"unknown\" rather than silently ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1626
msgid ""
"reference-type slugs to filter by, as returned by list-filters. Several "
"slugs in one axis are combined with OR; different axes with AND."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1632
msgid "reference-filter-1 slugs to filter by."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1638
msgid "reference-filter-2 slugs to filter by."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1644
msgid "Customer post IDs to filter by, as returned by list-filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1650
msgid "Location post IDs to filter by, as returned by list-filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1656
msgid ""
"Free-text search over the reference TITLE only. It is WordPress core search, "
"which reads post_title, post_excerpt and post_content — and this plugin "
"holds the descriptive text in ACF fields with post_content empty, so a term "
"appearing in the short description will NOT be found here, and an empty "
"result is not evidence that nothing matches. To search those, filter by the "
"axes that are indexed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1660
msgid "Page number, starting at 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1666
msgid "References per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1673
msgid ""
"Direction of the date component of the sort. Featured references always sort "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1683
msgid ""
"The filters as REQUESTED, after normalisation. This describes the request, "
"not the executed query: a site callback on pre_get_posts can rewrite paging, "
"ordering or the search term afterwards, and this ability cannot vouch for a "
"window it did not see."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1684
msgid ""
"Requested values that match nothing on this site, keyed by axis. A non-empty "
"value explains why a result set is empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1685
msgid "Total number of listed references matching the filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1686
msgid "The page that was returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1687
msgid "The page size that was applied after clamping."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1688
msgid "Number of pages available for these filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1689
msgid "Front-end archive URL for references, empty when there is none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1690 includes/abilities.php:1724
msgid "Locale this answer was read in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1691
msgid "The matching references for the requested page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1692
msgid ""
"How many records on this page were dropped because their stored data could "
"not be read. Normally 0; a non-zero value means the page holds fewer records "
"than per_page for a site-side reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1702
msgid "Get one reference"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1703
msgid ""
"Returns one reference by ID, including the detail data its page publishes: "
"the short description and the image gallery. A reference that no listing "
"contains is still resolvable here, together with whether it is listed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1714
msgid ""
"Reference post ID, as returned by jpkcom-acf-references/query-references."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1723
msgid ""
"Whether the public listing contains this reference. Answered by running the "
"listing rule restricted to this one ID, not by re-deriving it, so it cannot "
"disagree with jpkcom-acf-references/query-references."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1727
msgid ""
"Why no detail block is present. \"redirects_externally\" when an external "
"URL sends every visitor away before the page renders, \"expired\" when the "
"page redirects to the archive. In both states the description and the "
"gallery of this reference were never published to anybody, so they are "
"withheld here too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1731
msgid ""
"Detail data, present only for a reference whose page actually renders for an "
"anonymous visitor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1733
msgid "The short description as plain text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1736
msgid "Gallery images, as URL and alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1740
msgid "Image URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1741
